<p>President Trump is pressing allies and other major oil-importing countries to help secure and reopen the Strait of Hormuz after Iranian attacks disrupted shipping in the vital waterway during the third week of the U.S.-Israeli war on Iran. U.S. officials are trying to assemble a multinational escort coalition that could be announced this week. Trump has also warned NATO allies of a &quot;very bad&quot; future if they do not assist, and said he could delay a planned summit with Chinese President Xi Jinping to push Beijing to help. The early response from partners has been cautious. Japan and Australia said they have no current plans to send naval vessels, and reports said the UK is leaning toward surveillance and diplomacy instead of joining a naval deployment. Even so, the diplomatic push shows countries are still weighing ways to keep one of the world’s most important energy routes open — a sign that, despite the sharp rhetoric, the focus remains on preventing a wider disruption to trade and oil supplies.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/iJ4YMFpqBsGEmDERK1Ht6WaToUoEBDB_VxTo7cjpuDw4e_MA8uSYErPp_4KO442zhFTlI5xzSjDfp0wjzvWDv5jYlfaJbxtw9NzYIC3k1DQmH2allAYsEl2pVOpjT5s_m9rlIpk5IhIET4KnYDSrNaF1V-y6KPyYkwejcZKO1m2vG19ziTAS125eyXKmFR5uXfTOZpXcOTCeFov_DD2Fg2n5UW_-lp-ISjP2qS8qj38MjsnW' alt='President Trump in the White House on Thursday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Seven countries: Trump said his administration had contacted about seven countries about joining the effort, and he publicly named China, France, Japan, South Korea and Britain among those he hoped would participate.</li><li>Burden-sharing message: Trump framed Hormuz security as a test of whether major oil importers would keep relying on Washington to police the waterway, widening the dispute from a military request into a broader argument over who should pay.</li><li>Energy strain: The disruption has pushed oil prices higher, and U.S. Energy Secretary Chris Wright said energy prices could remain elevated as the conflict continues.</li><li>Pressure tactic: Trump said the United States would &quot;remember&quot; countries that refused to help secure Hormuz, signaling that the appeal could carry diplomatic consequences beyond the immediate shipping crisis.</li></ul><blockquote>I think China should help too because China gets 90% of its oil from the Straits - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Japan: Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi said Tokyo had made no decision on dispatching escort ships and wanted to focus on what Japan could do within its legal framework while pursuing early de-escalation. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/16/iran-war-live-updates-news-oil-trump-hormuz-dubai-airport-israel-targets'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Australia: Australia said it had no plans to send navy vessels to the Middle East for Hormuz escorts, signaling reluctance to deepen its direct military involvement. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/trump-demands-others-help-secure-strait-hormuz-japan-and-australia-say-no-plans'>Reuters via Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>United Kingdom: Reports said London favored drones and diplomacy over sending warships, showing support for maritime security without immediate naval escalation. (<a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/uk-japan-australia-reject-trumps-push-for-naval-coalition-in-strait-of-hormuz-13989892.html'>Firstpost</a>)</li><li>Iranian Revolutionary Guard: The force rejected the pressure campaign in blunt terms, signaling that Tehran would not be intimidated by outside naval deployments. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/15/muted-response-as-trump-urges-nations-to-escort-ships-through-hormuz-strait'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/trump-demands-others-help-secure-strait-hormuz-japan-and-australia-say-no-plans'>Trump demands others help secure Strait of Hormuz, Japan and Australia say no plans to send ships</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/trump-warns-nato-faces-very-bad-future-if-allies-fail-to-help-reopen-strait-of-hormuz-13989928.html'>Trump warns Nato faces ‘very bad’ future if allies fail to help reopen Strait of Hormuz</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/reactions-to-trumps-call-for-help-to-secure-strait-of-hormuz'>Reactions to Trump’s call for help to secure Strait of Hormuz</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/3d92284c-874e-42ce-8049-6b18e20eeb9c'>FirstFT: Trump warns European allies on Nato over Hormuz plea</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/15/muted-response-as-trump-urges-nations-to-escort-ships-through-hormuz-strait'>Muted response as Trump urges nations to escort ships through Hormuz Strait</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/16/watch-trump-warns-us-will-remember-countries-that-dont-help-secure-the-strait-of-hormuz'>Watch: Trump warns US ‘will remember’ countries that don’t help secure the Strait of Hormuz</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-15-0700/world-trump-wants-other-countries-help-reopen-strait-hormuz-might-not-be-so-easy'>Trump wants other countries to help reopen the Strait of Hormuz. That might not be so easy.</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/trump-urges-us-allies-to-send-warships-to-strait-of-%E2%80%8Bhormuz-as-iran-vows-to-retaliate'>Trump demands that &#x27;about 7&#x27; countries join coalition to police Iran&#x27;s Strait of Hormuz</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3346692/starmer-holds-calls-trump-and-carney-irans-hormuz-blockage'>Trump warns he ‘may delay’ China visit in demand for countries to secure Hormuz</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/15/world/iran-